{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And let us confound.</b> And let us confuse — an expression of something mixed, from the root of ״בלולה בשמן״ (Leviticus 2:5)." "<b>So that no one will hear his fellow's language.</b> That each and every one will forget all the languages except one, and what this one knows, that one will not know; but all together they will know seventy languages. And one should not explain that at that time seventy languages were created — is that not already known?"], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:03:50.636747942Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}